#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364277 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "06c1ce9a-bad7-50d6-b6c7-a1423ccce4bb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Geometric Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c85153c-eb9f-550b-b019-defd84334f28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364279} {:answer/id #uuid "5b503cab-5b6a-55a8-a286-2202aa79873e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364280} {:answer/id #uuid "ebee5405-1c8c-5d37-a7e3-207dadaf3e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364281} {:answer/id #uuid "aa51c0ad-dc04-575e-af4e-4abd53549441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364282} {:answer/id #uuid "c45850c2-8228-56b4-ba02-1015d5d01010" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b503cab-5b6a-55a8-a286-2202aa79873e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364280} :answer-field/id #uuid "4de825f7-0447-53f5-b85a-6e0112744178" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "181d1dda-5cff-574e-8975-8c6dc281393d" :question/math-academy-id "q-130486" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables follow a geometric distribution?\n\n- The number of files reviewed by an antivirus until the first infected file is found\n- The number of infected files found in a computer\n- The number of crayons randomly picked out from a case before a blue crayon is picked\n\nAssume independent trials with a constant success probability strictly between $0$ and $1$ for each experiment. Replace and mix each crayon before the next draw." :question/worked-solution "A geometric distribution models waiting for the first success in independent Bernoulli trials with constant success probability.\n\n- I counts file checks through the first infected file. Under the stated model, $P(T=k)=(1-p)^{k-1}p$ for $k=1,2,\\ldots$.\n- II counts the total infected files in a computer; it does not count trials until the first success.\n- III counts nonblue draws before the first blue crayon. Replacement keeps the probability of blue constant. Under the stated model, $P(F=k)=(1-q)^kq$ for $k=0,1,2,\\ldots$.\n\nI and III are geometric, using the trials and failures conventions respectively. The correct answer is \"I and III only.\"\n\nThe original source omits the independence and constant-probability assumptions and does not specify crayon replacement. Without replacement, III generally is not geometric; the study wording makes the intended model explicit."}]}
